= Metabolism — Simple =

'''Metabolism''' is the collection of chemical reactions happening inside living cells.

Some reactions break substances down, and others build new substances. Cells link these reactions to get energy and make the materials they need.

[[Enzyme|Enzymes]] help many reactions happen fast enough. Cells often use ATP and other molecules to transfer usable energy.

Metabolism is not just “burning calories.” Different organisms have different chemical pathways, and not all metabolism requires oxygen.

